U-TOT-000005</div><span class="status">FLAGSHIP CASE · PROVISIONAL FINDING</span></div><div class="console-actions"><a href="/truth/case-000005.php">OPEN FULL TRIAL ↗</a></div></div><div class="console-grid"><section class="claim-panel"><div class="panel-label">CLAIM UNDER REVIEW</div><h3>God bodily raised Jesus after his execution.</h3><blockquote>The early belief is historical data. Resurrection is an explanation of that data—not the datum itself.</blockquote><div class="tags"><span>HISTORY</span><span>TESTIMONY</span><span>PHILOSOPHY</span><span>THEOLOGY</span></div></section><section class="verdict-panel"><div class="panel-label">PROVISIONAL TRUST-WORTHY FINDING</div><div class="verdict-big">EARLY BELIEF SECURE<br><em>DIVINE CAUSE NOT COMPELLED</em></div><p>Jesus’ crucifixion and very early resurrection belief are strongly supported. Experiences interpreted as appearances are strongly indicated. A bodily resurrection remains a serious cumulative explanation, but history alone cannot force the theological conclusion.</p><a class="micro-link" href="/truth/case-000005.php">WEIGH THE FULL EVIDENCE →</a></section><section class="matrix-panel"><div class="panel-label">EVIDENCE CONFIDENCE · NOT MIRACLE PROBABILITY</div><div class="verdict-big">KEEP THE LAYERS<br><em>SEPARATE</em></div><p class="matrix-note">The trial labels direct historical support, inference, dispute, philosophical judgment, and theology instead of turning them into one certainty score.</p><div class="meter-row"><span>CRUCIFIXION</span><b style="--p:96%"></b><em>STRONG</em></div><div class="meter-row"><span>EARLY RESURRECTION BELIEF</span><b style="--p:92%"></b><em>STRONG</em></div><div class="meter-row"><span>EMPTY-TOMB HISTORY</span><b style="--p:58%"></b><em>DISPUTED</em></div></section></div><div class="evidence-floor"><section class="network-panel"><div class="panel-label">EVIDENCE NETWORK // INTERACTIVE MODEL</div><div class="network" id="network"><span class="claim-node">CLAIM</span><button style="--x:14%;--y:28%" data-tip="Earliest primary texts">P</button><button style="--x:30%;--y:70%" data-tip="Appearance traditions">A</button><button style="--x:52%;--y:18%" data-tip="Empty-tomb dispute">T</button><button style="--x:72%;--y:67%" data-tip="Competing explanations">C</button><button style="--x:88%;--y:28%" data-tip="Miracle assumptions">M</button><svg viewBox="0 0 100 50" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M50 25 L14 14 M50 25 L30 35 M50 25 L52 9 M50 25 L72 34 M50 25 L88 14"/></svg><output id="nodeTip">Select an evidence node to inspect its role.</output></div></section><section class="findings-panel"><div class="panel-label">EVIDENTIARY STATES</div><ul class="findings"><li class="yes"><b>VERIFIED FACT</b><span>Early sources report resurrection belief and claimed appearances.</span></li><li class="warn"><b>INFERENCE</b><span>Experiences helped generate the movement’s conviction.</span></li><li class="info"><b>DISPUTED</b><span>The empty tomb and narrative independence remain contested.</span></li><li class="unknown"><b>THEOLOGY</b><span>“God raised Jesus” exceeds what the surviving reports directly establish.</span></li></ul></section></div></article></div></section><section class="section protocol"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">ANALYST PROTOCOL</div><h2>Every conclusion has to survive contact with its evidence.</h2></div></div><div class="protocol-grid"><article class="glass tilt"><b>01</b><h3>TRACE ORIGIN</h3><p>Move toward primary and earliest accessible evidence instead of treating repetition as corroboration.</p></article><article class="glass tilt"><b>02</b><h3>DECOMPOSE CLAIM</h3><p>Separate the literal assertion from implication, framing, emotional payload, and unstated assumptions.</p></article><article class="glass tilt"><b>03</b><h3>ATTACK THE THEORY</h3><p>Seek the strongest credible counterevidence and competing explanation before choosing a finding.</p></article><article class="glass tilt"><b>04</b><h3>SHOW THE CHAIN</h3><p>Label verified fact, inference, missing context, dispute, uncertainty and opinion distinctly.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="section" id="trials" style="scroll-margin-top:88px"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">CASE INDEX // PUBLISHED & OPEN</div><h2>Explore the evidence files.</h2></div><a class="micro-link" href="/truth/lab/">BUILD YOUR OWN CLAIM MAP →</a></div><div class="case-cards"><a class="case-card tilt" href="/truth/case-000005.php"><span>PU-TOT-000005 // FLAGSHIP OPEN</span><h3>Did Jesus really rise from the dead — or is there a better explanation?</h3><p>The earliest resurrection belief, appearances, empty-tomb tradition, contradictions and competing explanations are tested without blending history, inference and theology.</p><b>EXAMINE CASE →</b></a><a class="case-card tilt" href="/truth/case-000004.php"><span>PU-TOT-000004 // OPEN</span><h3>Did the CIA control the American media?</h3><p>Declassified records establish covert relationships and media activity—but not total control of the American press.</p><b>EXAMINE CASE →</b></a><a class="case-card tilt" href="/truth/case-000003.php"><span>PU-TOT-000003 // OPEN</span><h3>Who was Jesus — before religion told us who he was?</h3><p>Historical existence and supernatural claims are separated into different evidentiary questions.</p><b>EXAMINE CASE →</b></a><a class="case-card tilt" href="/truth/case-000001.php"><span>TW-CLAIM-000001 // PROVISIONAL</span><h3>Does God individually cause or permit every bad thing?</h3><p>Absolute theological conclusions are tested against the evidence rather than protected from it.</p><b>EXAMINE CASE →</b></a><a class="case-card tilt" href="/truth/case-000002.php"><span>TW-CLAIM-000002 // OPEN</span><h3>Did Jesus teach the modern Romans Road / sinner's prayer?</h3><p>A familiar formula is tested against recorded teaching, Romans itself, conversion history, and its strongest defense.</p><b>EXAMINE CASE →</b></a></div></div></section><section class="section final-cta"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">PROJECT UNVEILED // TRUTH ON TRIAL // POWERED BY TRUST-WORTHY</div><h2>BEFORE WE ACT, LET'S KNOW.</h2><p>Bring a claim. Inspect the chain. Challenge the finding. Change the conclusion when better evidence wins.</p><a class="button pulse" href="#investigate">TRY TRUST-WORTHY NOW →</a><p class="privacy-copy">Free trials are AI-assisted preliminary syntheses. Probability scores are provisional until validated through outcome calibration. They are not substitutes for authenticated primary-source research. <a href="/privacy.html#free-truth-trial-privacy">Read the privacy boundary.</a></p></div></section></main><footer class="footer"><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><strong>PROJECT UNVEILED</strong><span>TRUTH ON TRIAL · POWERED BY TRUST-WORTHY</span></div><nav><a href="#investigate">Investigate</a><a href="#trials">Cases</a><a href="/truth/lab/">Evidence Lab</a><a href="/privacy.html">Privacy</a></nav></div></footer></body></html>
